 S. C. 572, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1306039\"><a href=\"/opinion/1306039/state-v-copeland/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State v. Copeland\">300 S. E. 2d 63</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9039656,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":577,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b1192-8\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"An5a\">dissenting. Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}